{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793039680,"nonce":"Om1WMP9AbK4KceljbGfCQAuwQS4=","title":"Persist hosted filesystem write payloads before compute execution","message":"Automatic compute recovery needs durable bytes for direct writes as well as document CRDT records. Add private workspace-scoped R2 objects referenced from the existing ordered mutation ledger. Reserve a bounded, deduplicated payload quota together with the pending intent before upload; execute compute only after the checksum-verified object is available. Failed uploads must never reach compute, and possible uploaded objects must remain accounted for. Keep immutable objects across overwrite/delete for ordered recovery; reclaim/retention remains a separate milestone.\n\nProvide a private owner/source/revision-checked operation-payload export, never a public route or bucket URL. Verify length and digest on reuse and export. Keep pending/uncertain/refused operations out of committed-payload export. Missing bindings, corrupt or missing objects and stale plans fail closed. Account/workspace isolation, binary/Unicode/empty files, dedup, object restart, compute destruction, upload failures and quota refusal before side effects need integration coverage.\n\nThis is filesystem operation payload durability, not a complete filesystem manifest or automatic VM recovery. Initial checkout/Git index, external/program writes, saved-vs-dirty restoration, stable identities, leases/fencing, materialization and the MSB provider remain under 52138fcda83502ec87679713955f7cf7c7f7e8654a0ef55ba60357bd0f22a904 and 670bd15d5f2a4c8fdd82da62e9b72599f9a689affc5682a7b621f81fd72156c0. Keep automaticRestore:false. Rebuild WASM and session and refresh local services at this checkpoint.","files":null}]}